extends SceneTree
## Bakes the building pictures into art/building_atlas.png and art/building_atlas.json: one row of 16 x 16 pictures, drawn here
## as text rows you can nudge. In the text-glyph look a building is its letter. A picture is see-through where it has no pixel, so
## the ground shows around it, and each has a dark outline so it stands apart from whatever ground it is on.
##
## Run from the project folder, then re-import:
##     godot --headless --path . -s res://tools/make_buildings.gd
##     godot --headless --path . --import
##
## Letters: k ink (outline), K dark brown, w white, W light grey, s stone, d dark grey, y gold, Y dark gold, o orange, r red,
## R dark red, t tan wood, T dark wood, g green, G dark green, b blue, B dark blue, c cyan, p purple, P dark purple.

